{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788225917,"nonce":"cbwZVp8DOjCbCCbs3a4bZhbMUIg=","message":"GOES FIRST, and the composition layer above it is now filed separately as `bac4eba` — session 11 (`65b03c2`), 2026-08-31.\n\nEvan resolved base composition this session: **a 7x7 module grid**, rooms being one module or a subdivision of one (quarters, halves, corner shapes), because a base is connected rooms rather than separate huts. He then sequenced it: **this issue first, as already specced, because it is the fleshed-out one** — prove `place-layout` puts ONE room down correctly before building a tiling layer on it.\n\nTwo things from that decision that bear on this issue's own scope, recorded here so they are not a surprise later:\n\n1. **This spec has no composition rule at all**, and the corpus shows it: the three shipped templates are **5x7, 11x6 and 7x7** (`templates/INDEX.md`) and no two of them tile. `place-layout {file} --origin P` places islands. That is fine for this issue's rehearsal and is exactly why it can go first — but the acceptance rehearsal is a **5x7** bedroom, which is off the agreed module. Either re-cut it to 7x7 (or a subdivision), or state plainly that the rehearsal deliberately exercises the non-modular path.\n2. **`power-room` is already 7x7**, so the module is not new — it is the one the corpus half-adopted without saying so.\n\nAlso worth pinning while this issue is being worked, because `bac4eba` depends on it: `templates/INDEX.md` records that **\"Row 0 = north is PROPOSED, not established — 3.3 pins it.\"** A grid makes that urgent, since phase is meaningless without a fixed orientation. Pinning it here costs nothing; leaving it unpinned makes the grid ambiguous.","files":null}]}